        ],
        "context": "example",
        "id": null,
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "The body will usually be provided as a value object to be rendered to a corresponding response representation (for example, JSON) by one of the registered "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "HttpMessageConverters"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "A "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "ResponseEntity<Resource>"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " can be returned for file content, copying the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "InputStream"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " content of the provided resource to the response "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "OutputStream"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ". Note that the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "InputStream"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " should be lazily retrieved by the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Resource"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " handle in order to reliably close it after it has been copied to the response. If you are using "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "InputStreamResource"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " for such a purpose, make sure to construct it with an on-demand "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "InputStreamSource"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " (for example, through a lambda expression that retrieves the actual "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "InputStream"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "). Also, custom subclasses of "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "InputStreamResource"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " are only supported in combination with a custom "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "contentLength()"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " implementation which avoids consuming the stream for that purpose."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Spring MVC supports using a single value "
          },
          {
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "reactive type"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "xref",
            "target": "web/webmvc/mvc-ann-async.html#mvc-ann-async-reactive-types"
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " to produce the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "ResponseEntity"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " asynchronously, and/or single and multi-value reactive types for the body. This allows the following types of async responses:"
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "ulist",
        "id": null,
        "items": [
          {
            "blocks": [],
            "checkbox": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "ResponseEntity<Mono<T>>"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " or "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "ResponseEntity<Flux<T>>"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " make the response status and headers known immediately while the body is provided asynchronously at a later point. Use "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Mono"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " if the body consists of 0..1 values or "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Flux"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " if it can produce multiple values."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "blocks": [],
            "checkbox": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Mono<ResponseEntity<T>>"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " provides all three — response status, headers, and body, asynchronously at a later point. This allows the response status and headers to vary depending on the outcome of asynchronous request handling."
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "style": null,
        "title": null
      }
    ],
